// hello1.lyr
//
// Welcome to lyriclings. Every exercise is a small Lyric program with something wrong in it.
// Your job: make it compile, run and print what the exercise expects.
//
// A Lyric program starts at `main`, which returns the process exit code. `println` lives in
// the standard library module `std.io.console`; nothing from the standard library is in scope
// until you import it.                                          (spec §4.2, guide chapter 1)
//
// Run this exercise as it is to see what the compiler says, then fix it and remove the line
// below that says the exercise is not done.
//
// Expected output:
//   Hello, Lyric!

// I AM NOT DONE

fn main(): int {
    println("Hello, Lyric!");
    return 0;
}
